DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261110T061500
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261110T071000
SUMMARY:W13D2 SWIM | 2500 yd | aerobic + buoy comparison
DESCRIPTION:W13D2 — TUESDAY SWIM | 2500 yd | 25-yard pool\nGOAL: Aerobic 
 endurance and compare buoy vs unassisted swimming.\n01 | WARM-UP — 400 y
 d\n400 easy freestyle\, NO equipment\; relaxed breathing.\nRest 30 sec bef
 ore drills.\n02 | TECHNIQUE — 4 x 50 yd = 200 yd\n#1-2: 25 catch-up dril
 l + 25 easy freestyle\, NO equipment.\n#3-4: 25 fingertip drag + 25 easy f
 reestyle\, NO equipment.\nRest 20 sec after EACH 50\; 30 sec before main s
 et.\n03 | MAIN SET — 4 x 300 yd = 1200 yd\n#1: NO equipment\; smooth aer
 obic\, RPE 4-5.\n#2: PULL BUOY only\; same effort\, compare pace and strok
 es.\n#3: NO equipment\; same effort\, compare with #1.\n#4: NO equipment\;
  controlled technique\, RPE 5.\nRest 30 sec after EACH 300\; 45 sec before
  next set.\n04 | CONTROLLED AEROBIC — 4 x 100 yd = 400 yd\nAll NO equipm
 ent\; even relaxed pace\, RPE 4-5.\nRest 20 sec after EACH 100\; 30 sec be
 fore cooldown.\n05 | COOLDOWN — 6 x 50 yd = 300 yd\nAll NO equipment\; v
 ery easy freestyle or backstroke.\nRest 15 sec after EACH 50.\nTOTAL: 400 
 + 200 + 1200 + 400 + 300 = 2500 yd.\nEQUIPMENT: Pull buoy ONLY for main-se
 t 300 #2. NO paddles or fins.\nCALF: Gentle push-offs\; avoid hard kicking
 . Record split and stroke count for all 300s.\nRest times are between repe
 ats\; no extra rest needed after final cooldown.
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
