SUMMARY:W13D7 SWIM | 1800 yd | easy technique
DESCRIPTION:W13D7 — SUNDAY SWIM | 1800 yd | 25-yard pool\nGOAL: Easy tech
 nique swim before recovery bike + return-to-run.\n01 | WARM-UP — 300 yd\
 n300 easy freestyle\, NO equipment\; RPE 2-3.\nRest 30 sec before drills.\
 n02 | TECHNIQUE — 6 x 50 yd = 300 yd\n#1-2: 25 catch-up + 25 easy freest
 yle\, NO equipment.\n#3-4: 25 fingertip drag + 25 easy freestyle\, NO equi
 pment.\n#5-6: relaxed bilateral breathing practice\, NO equipment.\nRest 2
 0 sec after EACH 50\; 30 sec before main set.\n03 | MAIN SET — 4 x 250 y
 d = 1000 yd\n#1: NO equipment\; relaxed aerobic RPE 3-4.\n#2: PULL BUOY on
 ly\; same effort\, compare pace and strokes.\n#3: NO equipment\; compare w
 ith #1.\n#4: NO equipment\; smooth\, easy form RPE 3-4.\nRest 30 sec after
  EACH 250\; 30 sec before cooldown.\n04 | COOLDOWN — 4 x 50 yd = 200 yd\
 nAll NO equipment\; very easy RPE 2.\nRest 15 sec after EACH 50.\nTOTAL: 3
 00 + 300 + 1000 + 200 = 1800 yd.\nEQUIPMENT: Pull buoy ONLY for main-set 2
 50 #2. NO paddles or fins.\nCALF: Gentle push-offs\; minimal kicking effor
 t.\nIMPORTANT: Save energy for today's bike + run/walk\; no hard swim inte
 rvals.
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
